{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792490258,"nonce":"WhNxN5OjYVnSZg88K6y1pXYdXnA=","message":"Checked the air part. optimized_with_config keeps recent optimized bodies under a fixed 8 MiB strong budget (air_cache::BodyCache); an evicted body survives only while the interpreter's prepared bodies, an OSR plan or a compile still hold it. So the 4.5 MB of Function::shrink_to_fit in the diff is that bounded cache, not growth per tab: it stops rising at about 8 MiB however many files open. Cranelift's 4.8 MB is the installed code and its per-function records for functions that ran, which grow with the number of distinct functions executed, not with open tabs. ASH_AIR_CACHE_STATS=1 prints the resident and live counts if the exact split matters. Lowering the budget would trade the floor for recomputing bodies the tiers ask for again (the pipeline is the expensive part); not changed.","files":null}]}